<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Rharhabe Xhosa Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1775 CE – 1847 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western Xhosa kingdom between the Kei and Fish rivers, which bore the brunt of the frontier wars with the Cape Colony.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rharhabe, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalo">Phalo</a>, quarrelled with his brother <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gcaleka-xhosa-kingdom">Gcaleka</a> and led followers west of the Kei, founding a separate kingdom when the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/xhosa-kingdom">Xhosa Kingdom</a> split around 1775. His successors ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xhosa-people">Xhosa</a> closest to the advancing Cape frontier.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was weakened by rivalry between the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndlambe">Ndlambe</a> and Rharhabe's grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngqika">Ngqika</a>, who sought British support; Ndlambe's forces defeated Ngqika at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-amalinde">Battle of Amalinde</a> in 1818. Under Ngqika's sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maqoma">Maqoma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandile">Sandile</a>, the Rharhabe fought repeated frontier wars, losing land as the Cape pushed its border from the Fish to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keiskamma-river">Keiskamma</a> and beyond.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the War of the Axe, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> annexed the territory between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keiskamma-river">Keiskamma</a> and Kei as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-kaffraria">British Kaffraria</a> in 1847, ending Rharhabe independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandile">Sandile</a> was killed in 1878 during the last frontier war.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1775 CE – 1847 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24